{"body":"## Summary\n- Behavior mode was executing source SQL with no connection-visibility principal, so private oauth_account feeds (e.g. personal X) silently vanished from Behavior windows even when `query_sql` as the owner showed them.\n- Interactive `knowledge.read` keeps the verified caller principal; signed Behavior-run sessions and scheduled fingerprints use the durable Behavior author (not a possibly-different agent owner).\n- Headless/fallback path: `userId ?? created_by`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `make pre-pr` clean (build + typecheck + knip + lint + exposed-surface naming)\n- [x] Focused unit visibility tests passed during review-fix\n- [x] `make review-fix` applied and committed (integration test added for interactive / Behavior-run / headless / fingerprint)\n- [ ] Integration test not run here (sandbox/EPERM on embedded Postgres) — CI will cover\n- [ ] Bug fix: red→fix→green outputs pasted below\n\n### Red (prod repro, before fix)\n```\nquery_sql: 23 x:tweet on Jul 30\nknowledge.read behavior_id=71 since/until=2026-07-30: recent_social = 10 linkedin:post only\n```\n\n### Fix\nPass principal into Behavior `queryContentData` / events CTE visibility; Behavior runs force author via `BEHAVIOR_RUN_SOURCE → userId: null → created_by`.\n\n### Green\nUnit visibility principal tests green locally; integration coverage added for CI.\n\n## Notes\nNo workarounds: no org-visibility widening of personal oauth connections (DB guard forbids it). This is the proper principal plumbing.\n\n\u003c!-- codesmith:footer --\u003e\n---\n\u003ca href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/lobu-ai/codesmith/lobu/pr/2354\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v2.svg\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v2.svg\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v2.svg\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003csup\u003eNeed help on this PR? Tag \u003ccode\u003e@codesmith-bot\u003c/code\u003e with what you need. Autofix is enabled.\u003c/sup\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- codesmith:autofix:enabled --\u003e\n\u003c!-- /codesmith:footer --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai --\u003e\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved private-connection visibility for Behavior runs by propagating the correct visibility principal through content querying and metric execution.\n  * Headless Behavior-mode handling now supports explicit `userId` context and uses the durable Behavior author for visibility where applicable.\n  * Added strict validation to prevent a Behavior run from accessing content tied to a different `behavior_id` (fails closed).\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added integration coverage for Behavior private-connection visibility and fingerprint stability.\n  * Added unit tests for visibility principal resolution and invalid Behavior-run identity cases.\n\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai --\u003e","mergeCommit":"85bedf0f08cdd34c52ea843f7bf5e885de76db2e","mergedAt":"2026-07-30T13:21:14Z","number":2354,"state":"MERGED","title":"fix(server): pass connection-visibility principal into Behavior knowledge.read","url":"https://github.com/lobu-ai/lobu/pull/2354"}
